# Compiler documentation and TDD

Follow @AGENTS.md as the repository-wide authority.

In particular, read @specs/DOCUMENTATION_STYLE.md before changing technical
documentation or source comments, and follow @specs/TDD_WORKFLOW.md for every
behavior-changing implementation. Use Red–Green–Refactor, preserve unrelated work, and
run the validation commands required by the affected subsystem.

Before implementing a new feature, require its issue in the `clojure-compiler Roadmap`,
run `make agent-feature-guard ISSUE=<issue-number>`, create
`feature/<issue-number>-<semantic-description>` from `master`, and deliver it through a
pull request to `master` as specified by @AGENTS.md. Do not implement missing
estimates, epics, roll-ups, or issues above 8 story points; refine them into independent
tasks first.
